.TH BALAI 1 "2026" "BalOS 1.0" "BalOS Manual"
.SH NAME
balai \- local offline AI assistant for BalOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B balai
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B balai
"\fIquestion\fR"
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBbalai\fR is a command-line wrapper around the local
.I ollama
HTTP daemon at 127.0.0.1:11434, pre-loaded with a Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct
Q4_K_M model (~1 GB, baked into the squashfs at ISO build time).

Nothing ever leaves the machine: no API keys, no cloud, no telemetry.
The systemd drop-in pins
.B OLLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1:11434 ,
.B OLLAMA_NO_CLOUD=true ,
and
.B OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=15m .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "" " (no arg)"
Launch the interactive chat REPL. Type \fI/clear\fR to reset, \fI/model\fR
to switch, \fI/help\fR for meta commands. Exit with \fI/exit\fR or Ctrl-D.
.TP
.BI "\"" question "\""
One-shot query. Streams the answer and exits.
.TP
.BI "cmd \"" intent "\""
Translate intent into ONE shell command. Shows the suggestion, blocks
destructive patterns via the shared
.B is_destructive
regex (see
.BR "" "SAFETY" "),"
and asks for confirmation before running.
.TP
.BI "agent \"" goal "\""
Iterative approval loop. The model proposes ONE command at a time,
you hit Enter (run) / s (skip) / q (quit) / e (edit). Output is fed
back into the next turn so the model can reason about results. Ends
on
.B DONE:
or
.B ABORT:
markers or after
.B BALAI_AGENT_MAX_STEPS
(default 10) iterations.
.TP
.BR "explain " [\fIfile | --last | --diff A B\fR]
Explain a file, the last shell history command, piped stdin, or the
semantic difference between two files.
.TP
.BR "fix " [\fIerror text\fR]
Diagnose an error and suggest a concrete fix. Stdin is accepted.
.TP
.B ctx
Dump the live system context that balai would inject for a
state-aware question (power profile, firewall tier, battery, VPN,
WiFi, kernel, uptime).
.TP
.B doctor
Gather diagnostics (failed systemd units, journal errors, disk
pressure, .pacnew files, pacman log tail) and produce a
one-paragraph AI verdict.
.TP
.B tip
One-line proactive suggestion based on the current snapshot. Also
shown in
.B bal status
(aka
.BR "balmonitor --once ")
footer.
.TP
.BI "remember \"" fact "\""
Append a persistent note that is prepended to every future prompt.
Stored at
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/balai/notes.md
(or ~/.local/state/balai/notes.md).
.TP
.B memory
Show all remembered notes.
.TP
.BR "forget " [\fIpattern\fR]
Drop notes matching a pattern (or wipe all with confirmation).
.TP
.BR "model " [\fIlist|pull|rm|default\fR]
Manage local models.
.TP
.B status
Service + model health + RAM usage.
.TP
.B setup
Re-run first-run setup (enable systemd service, pull default model).
.SH CONTEXT AWARENESS
When a query mentions words like
.I my , current , what's my
and a system concept (battery, firewall, VPN, …), balai prepends a
short
.B "Current BalOS system state:"
block before sending the prompt. The model is instructed to answer
from that block rather than guessing. Override with:
.TP
.B BALAI_CTX_MODE=auto
Default — inject only when the query looks stateful.
.TP
.B BALAI_CTX_MODE=always
Always inject.
.TP
.B BALAI_CTX_MODE=never
Never inject.
.SH SAFETY
.B balai cmd
and
.B balai agent
share a destructive-command blocklist (see
.B is_destructive
in the script). Refused patterns include:
.BR "rm -rf /... " "/"
.BR "rm -rf /home " ","
.BR "dd of=/dev/sdX " ","
.BR "mkfs " ","
.BR "curl ... | bash " ","
fork bombs,
.BR "chmod 777 / " ","
.BR "killall -9 systemd " ","
.B cryptsetup erase
and more. Refused commands are not run; they are optionally copied to
your clipboard so you can inspect them.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BALAI_MODEL
Override the default model (e.g. \fBqwen2.5:3b-instruct-q4_K_M\fR).
.TP
.B BALAI_SYSTEM_PROMPT
Path to a custom system prompt file.
.TP
.B BALAI_CTX_MODE
\fBauto\fR | \fBalways\fR | \fBnever\fR. See CONTEXT AWARENESS.
.TP
.B BALAI_AGENT_MAX_STEPS
Upper bound for the agent loop (default 10).
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
host:port of the ollama daemon (default 127.0.0.1:11434).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/bin/balai
Main CLI.
.TP
.B /usr/bin/balai-chat
Graphical Qt6 chat window (see
.BR balai-chat (1)).
.TP
.B /usr/share/balos/ai/system-prompt.md
System prompt injected on every turn.
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/balai/history.jsonl
Chat history (wiped by
.BR "bal panic soft ").
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/balai/notes.md
Remembered notes (wiped by
.BR "bal panic soft ").
.TP
.B /run/balos/{power-profile,shield-tier}
Live-state files consumed by
.BR "balai ctx ".
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bal (1),
.BR ollama (1),
.BR balpanic (1)
.SH AUTHOR
BalOS project.
